course: dictionary
lesson: 14036
title: Manipulate: control, handle or trick
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Manipulate has several meanings, so read the words around it to find the right one. Most often it means to control or influence someone in a clever, unfair or dishonest way to get what you want. «Sam said he would only be her friend if she gave him all her sweets. He was manipulating her.» The unfair deal and the threat show that manipulate means tricking her.
explain: Manipulate can also mean to handle something skilfully with your hands. «Ben manipulated the joystick to steer the boat through the rocks.» Here there is no trickery at all. The words joystick and steer show that manipulate means working a machine with care and skill.
explain: Look at the clues to decide. If the sentence is about people, it usually means trick or control. If it is about numbers, pictures or machines, it may mean change or handle. Try your meaning in the sentence: does «Sam was tricking her» still make sense? Then manipulate fits.
fact: Manipulate is a verb. Its forms are manipulates, manipulated and manipulating.
fact: «Manipulate» means to control or influence someone in a clever, unfair or dishonest way, to get what you want.
fact: «Manipulate» can mean to handle or move something skilfully with your hands, as in «manipulate the controls».
fact: «Manipulate» can mean to change information, numbers or pictures to trick people, as in «manipulate a photo». In maths, it can mean rearranging numbers or equations.
fact: A friend who tricks you into keeping secrets or doing what they want is manipulating you. Tell a trusted adult.
exercise: «Mia kept saying nobody liked Lily, so Lily gave Mia her lunch every day.» What is Mia doing? | Reading a book about lunch | *Manipulating Lily to get what she wants | Sharing her lunch with a friend | Drawing a map of the school
exercise: «Ben manipulated the joystick to steer the boat.» What does manipulated mean here? | Painted it bright blue | Forgot how it worked | Broke it on purpose | *Handled it skilfully with his hands
exercise: «The editor manipulated the photo so the lake looked bigger than it was.» What does manipulated mean? | Moved it gently into a box | Printed it in colour | *Changed it to trick people | Washed it clean
test: «The advert manipulated the numbers to make the product look better.» Which word is closest in meaning to manipulated? | Shared | Counted | Forgot | *Twisted
test: «She tried to ___ her little brother into doing all her chores.» Which word fits the gap? | *Manipulate | Measured | Thanked | Helped
exam: Lena says manipulate only means to move something with your hands. Is she right? | Yes, it only ever means to move something with your hands | *No, it can also mean to control someone unfairly or to change information to trick people | No, it means to sing a song | Yes, and it has no other meanings at all
